#!/usr/bin/python3
# Generated by Ask CK PyTest Creator for AWPTCM-T44297 — (261) Management_LLDP - LLDP-TLV
# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - All optional TLVs available in the LLDP TLV set — port description, system name,
#   system description, system capabilities and management address — are individually
#   selectable and individually clearable on a per-port basis.
#   - Selecting the complete set of optional TLVs on a transmitting port results in every
#   selected TLV being present in each transmitted LLDPDU, in addition to the mandatory
#   TLVs.
#   - With LLDP enabled and no optional TLVs selected, transmitted LLDPDUs carry only the
#   mandatory TLVs (chassis ID, port ID, time-to-live) and the end-of-LLDPDU marker, and no
#   optional TLV appears on the wire.
#   - Each single-instance optional TLV appears at most once in any single LLDPDU — no
#   LLDPDU carries duplicate port description, system name, system description or system
#   capabilities TLVs.
#   - At least one management address TLV is present in every transmitted LLDPDU when
#   management address transmission is selected; where multiple management addresses are
#   associated with the port, multiple management address TLVs may be carried in one LLDPDU.
#   - Management address TLV contents reflect the management address actually configured on
#   the device, and change to match when that address changes.
#   - The content of every transmitted TLV matches the corresponding locally configured or
#   locally derived value as reported by the device's own management interfaces.
#   - The per-port TLV transmit-enable state held in the LLDP management information base
#   agrees with the state selected through the command interface, port by port and TLV by
#   TLV.
#   - Per-port independence holds: TLV selections applied to one port do not alter the TLVs
#   transmitted on any other port, including ports with no optional TLVs selected.
#   - Optional TLV selection takes effect on a transmit-only port with the same result as on
#   a transmit-and-receive port; receive capability is not a precondition for TLV
#   transmission.
#   - The LLDP-MED TLV set is separately selectable from the basic optional TLV set, and MED
#   TLV selections are reflected in transmitted LLDPDUs as the standards-defined
#   organisationally specific TLVs.
#   - MED capability and network policy TLV contents conform to the defined TLV format and
#   carry values consistent with the device's MED configuration.
#   - Selecting or clearing a TLV while LLDP is running takes effect on subsequent LLDPDUs
#   without requiring LLDP or the port to be restarted, and without disrupting transmission
#   of the remaining TLVs.
#   - An attempt to select an unsupported, misspelled or out-of-range TLV keyword is
#   rejected with a diagnostic message, and the previously configured TLV selection is left
#   unchanged.
#   - TLV selection commands on a port with LLDP disabled are accepted and retained as
#   configuration, and become effective when LLDP is subsequently enabled.
#   - Repeating a selection already in effect, or clearing a TLV that is already deselected,
#   is accepted without error and leaves the resulting state unchanged.
#   - TLV selection state is reported by the device's operational display commands, per
#   port, distinguishing selected from unselected TLVs.
#   - TLV selection state appears in the saved and displayed running configuration in a form
#   that restores the same selections after a device restart.
#   - A neighbour device receiving the LLDPDUs reports exactly the set of optional TLVs
#   selected on the transmitting port, and reports no information for TLVs that were not
#   selected.
#   - LLDP frame and TLV counters remain consistent across TLV selection changes, with no
#   increment of error, malformed-frame or discarded-TLV counters attributable to a valid
#   TLV selection.
# ==================================================================

